        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Uhud</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">Saturday, 23 March 625 (7 Shawwal, 3 AH)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">A valley north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a> near Mount Uhud, in present-day Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> under Abu Sufyan ibn Harb, with a force of approximately 3,000 men, 700 of them in chain mail; the early Muslims under Muhammad, 1,000 men at first and around 700 after 300 withdrew, of whom 100 had chain mail</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Muslims suffered heavy losses, among them Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and the Meccans withdrew without pressing home their advantage; scholars differ on whether this was a Muslim defeat or an indecisive result.</span></div>
