    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Muhammad posted 50 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a> on a hill to guard the Muslim rear against the Meccan cavalry; when most of them went down to join the advance, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalid-ibn-al-walid">Khalid ibn al-Walid</a>'s cavalry attacked the flank and rear.</li><li>Ibn al-Athir names 85 Muslims killed, 75 of them Medinans and 10 Emigrants from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>.</li><li>Chase F. Robinson calls the Muslim defeat clear enough, while William Montgomery Watt notes that the Meccans failed to achieve their aim of destroying Muhammad and his followers.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Abu Sufyan shouted from the mountain that victory in war goes by turns and that this day was in exchange for the day of Badr, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umar-ibn-al-khattab">Umar ibn al-Khattab</a> answered him by Muhammad's instruction.</p></aside>
    </section>

